module njd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The District of New Jersey's own civil periods and limits, computed under
// FRCP 6(a), which governs a period stated in a local rule. Motion papers
// run backward from the motion day the notice of motion designates (L.Civ.R.
// 7.1(c)-(d), 78.1). Rules that state no period this layer can count stay
// out: the Clerk's one extension of the time to answer, of at most 14 days
// (L.Civ.R. 6.1(b)), which lengthens an FRCP period rather than stating
// one; the court's own scheduling of the initial conference within 60 days
// of the first answer (L.Civ.R. 16.1(a)(1)); the earliest time to serve
// contention interrogatories, 60 days before the close of fact discovery
// (L.Civ.R. 33.1(d)), which runs from a date the scheduling order sets;
// dismissal of a case inactive for 90 days (L.Civ.R. 41.1(a)), a court
// action, not a filing period; the notice and hearing window for taxing
// costs before the Clerk (L.Civ.R. 54.1(d)), a range; L.Civ.R. 9.1, which
// was rescinded effective December 1, 2022; the habeas and section 2255
// periods and page limits (L.Civ.R. 81.2, 81.3), which belong to a habeas
// package; attorney admission and discipline (L.Civ.R. 101.1-104.1); the
// arbitration scheduling and exchange periods (L.Civ.R. 201.1(e)-(f)),
// mediation (L.Civ.R. 301.1); appeals from the bankruptcy court (L.Civ.R.
// 601.1-601.7), which belong to a bankruptcy appeal layer; and the Local
// Criminal Rules. The earlier D.N.J. outline's FRCP flow belongs to lit/frcp
// and lit/frap; its decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Foman v. Davis, Frow v. De La
// Vega, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Catlin, Bowles v. Russell, and in
// the Third and Fourth Circuits Phillips v. County of Allegheny, Fowler v.
// UPMC Shadyside, Poulis v. State Farm, Goines and Anderson v. Foundation
// for Advancement) are FRCP authority, and no reporter text is vendored, so
// they are removed here.
// A brief is limited to 40 "ordinary typed or printed pages", excluding the
// tables of contents and authorities, unless the Judge permits more before
// it is submitted (L.Civ.R. 7.2(b)); 30 pages in 12-point proportional type
// (L.Civ.R. 7.2(d)). The rule states the count in a form the limit check
// does not read, so the limit stays in this note.
/// A reply brief under L.Civ.R. 7.1(d)(3), and a brief for or against a
/// motion for reconsideration under L.Civ.R. 7.1(i): at most 15 pages,
/// excluding the tables (L.Civ.R. 7.2(b)); 11.25 pages in 12-point
/// proportional type (L.Civ.R. 7.2(d)).
limit reply-brief { pages <= 15 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.2(b)" } cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.2(b)"

/// The combined brief opposing a motion and supporting a cross-motion, and
/// the original movant's combined reply: at most 40 pages each (L.Civ.R.
/// 7.1(h)).
limit cross-motion-brief {
  pages <= 40 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.1(h)"
} cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.1(h)"

/// The motion day the notice of motion designates: the first regular motion
/// day at least 24 days after filing (L.Civ.R. 7.1(c)(1), 78.1).
event MotionDay()
/// The moving papers and brief are filed (L.Civ.R. 7.1(d)(1)).
event MotionBriefFiled()
/// The opposition brief is filed (L.Civ.R. 7.1(d)(2)).
event OppositionBriefFiled()
/// The reply brief is filed (L.Civ.R. 7.1(d)(3)).
event ReplyBriefFiled() paper reply-brief
/// A combined cross-motion brief is filed (L.Civ.R. 7.1(h)).
event CrossMotionBriefFiled() paper cross-motion-brief
/// The court rules on a motion (L.Civ.R. 7.1(e)).
event MotionRuled()
/// The order or judgment on a motion is entered (L.Civ.R. 7.1(i)).
event OrderEntered()
/// A party files its initial pleading, or the matter is transferred or
/// removed to this district (L.Civ.R. 7.1.1(a)).
event InitialPleadingFiled()
/// A written request for a statement of the damages claimed is served
/// (L.Civ.R. 8.1).
event DamagesRequestServed()
/// Counsel or an unrepresented party learns of a change of address
/// (L.Civ.R. 10.1(a)).
event AddressChangeLearned()
/// The order resolving a motion to dismiss fewer than all claims is entered
/// (L.Civ.R. 12.2).
event PartialDismissalOrderEntered()
/// The date of the initial scheduling conference (L.Civ.R. 26.1(b)(2)).
event InitialSchedulingConference()
/// The parties' initial Fed. R. Civ. P. 26(f) meeting (L.Civ.R.
/// 26.1(b)(2)).
event PartiesMeeting()
/// The 60-day order administratively terminating a settled case is entered
/// (L.Civ.R. 41.1(b)).
event AdministrativeTerminationEntered()
/// A judgment allowing costs is entered (L.Civ.R. 54.1(a)).
event CostsJudgmentEntered()
/// The Clerk acts on the bill of costs (L.Civ.R. 54.1(h)).
event CostsTaxed()
/// Judgment or an order allowing a counsel fee is entered (L.Civ.R.
/// 54.2(a)).
event FeeJudgmentEntered()
/// The court makes a judgment as defined in Fed. R. Civ. P. 54(a)
/// (L.Civ.R. 58.1(b)).
event JudgmentDetermined()
/// The court receives the prevailing party's proposed judgment or order
/// (L.Civ.R. 58.1(b)).
event ProposedJudgmentReceived()
/// A party is served with a magistrate judge's order on a non-dispositive
/// matter (L.Civ.R. 72.1(c)(1)(A)).
event MagistrateOrderServed()
/// A party is served with a magistrate judge's proposed findings,
/// recommendations or report (L.Civ.R. 72.1(c)(2)).
event MagistrateReportServed()
/// The final pretrial conference is held (L.Civ.R. 73.1(d)).
event FinalPretrialConference()
/// The arbitration award is filed and served, by a party under 28 U.S.C.
/// § 657(a) or by the Clerk, whichever occurs first (L.Civ.R. 201.1(h)).
event ArbitrationAwardServed()

/// L.Civ.R. 7.1(d)(1): no application is heard unless the moving papers, a
/// brief and proof of service are filed at least 24 days before the noticed
/// motion day.
deadline motion-papers-period: 24.days before MotionDay() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.1(d)"

/// L.Civ.R. 7.1(d)(2): the opposition brief and papers are filed at least
/// 14 days before the original motion day, unless the court orders
/// otherwise or the opponent of a dispositive motion takes the one
/// automatic adjournment under L.Civ.R. 7.1(d)(5), which moves the period to
/// 14 days before the new motion day.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days before MotionDay() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.1(d)"

/// L.Civ.R. 7.1(d)(3): a reply, if any, is filed at least seven days before
/// the motion day. No reply is filed without leave on a cross-motion,
/// reconsideration, case management or discovery motion.
deadline reply-period: 7.days before MotionDay() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.1(d)"

/// L.Civ.R. 7.1(e): if the proposed order annexed to the motion does not
/// reflect the ruling, the prevailing party, if directed, submits an order
/// within seven days of the ruling on notice to all parties.
deadline proposed-order-period: 7.days after MotionRuled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.1(e)"

/// L.Civ.R. 7.1(i): unless a statute or rule such as Fed. R. Civ. P. 50, 52
/// or 59 provides otherwise, a motion for reconsideration is served and
/// filed within 14 days after entry of the order or judgment on the
/// original motion.
deadline reconsideration-period: 14.days after OrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.1(i)"

/// L.Civ.R. 7.1.1(a): within 30 days of filing an initial pleading or of
/// transfer or removal of the matter to this district, each party files a
/// statement disclosing any non-party providing non-recourse litigation
/// funding.
deadline litigation-funding-disclosure-period: 30.days after InitialPleadingFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 7.1.1(a)"

/// L.Civ.R. 8.1: within 14 days after service of a written request, the
/// party pleading unliquidated damages furnishes a statement of the amount
/// claimed.
deadline damages-statement-period: 14.days after DamagesRequestServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 8.1"

/// L.Civ.R. 10.1(a): counsel and unrepresented parties file notice of a
/// change of their or their client's address within seven days of being
/// apprised of it.
deadline address-change-period: 7.days after AddressChangeLearned() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 10.1(a)"

/// L.Civ.R. 12.2: when a Fed. R. Civ. P. 12(b) motion addresses fewer than
/// all claims, the pleading in response to the claims not dismissed is
/// filed 14 days after entry of the order resolving the motion.
deadline remaining-claims-response-period: 14.days after PartialDismissalOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 12.2"

/// L.Civ.R. 26.1(b)(2): the initial Fed. R. Civ. P. 26(f) meeting is
/// convened at least 21 days before the initial scheduling conference.
deadline parties-meeting-period: 21.days before InitialSchedulingConference() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 26.1(b)"

/// L.Civ.R. 26.1(b)(2): the proposed discovery plan generated at the
/// meeting is delivered to the Magistrate Judge within 14 days after it.
deadline discovery-plan-period: 14.days after PartiesMeeting() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 26.1(b)"

/// L.Civ.R. 26.1(b)(2): unless stipulated or directed otherwise, initial
/// disclosures under Fed. R. Civ. P. 26(a)(1) are made within 14 days after
/// the initial meeting of the parties.
deadline initial-disclosures-period: 14.days after PartiesMeeting() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 26.1(b)"

/// L.Civ.R. 41.1(b): within 60 days after entry of the order
/// administratively terminating a settled case, counsel file the papers to
/// dismiss it under Fed. R. Civ. P. 41(a)(1)(A)(ii); otherwise the court
/// dismisses it with prejudice. The court may extend the period for good
/// cause.
deadline settlement-dismissal-period: 60.days after AdministrativeTerminationEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 41.1(b)"

/// L.Civ.R. 54.1(a), (e): within 30 days after entry of a judgment allowing
/// costs, or of the order disposing of the last timely post-trial motion,
/// the prevailing party serves and files a Bill of Costs and Disbursements;
/// failure waives all costs. The period from a post-trial order runs from
/// an event this layer does not model.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 30.days after CostsJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 54.1(a)"

/// L.Civ.R. 54.1(h): a dissatisfied party appeals the Clerk's taxation to
/// the court by notice of motion served within seven days of the Clerk's
/// action, as Fed. R. Civ. P. 54(d) provides.
deadline costs-review-period: 7.days after CostsTaxed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 54.1(h)"

/// L.Civ.R. 54.2(a): where a counsel fee is allowed by the court or
/// permitted by statute, the motion for fees and expenses is filed within
/// 30 days of entry of the judgment or order, unless the court extends it.
deadline fee-motion-period: 30.days after FeeJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 54.2(a)"

/// L.Civ.R. 58.1(b): in cases under Fed. R. Civ. P. 58(b)(2), the
/// prevailing party submits a judgment or order on notice within seven days
/// after the determination.
deadline proposed-judgment-period: 7.days after JudgmentDetermined() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 58.1(b)"

/// L.Civ.R. 58.1(b): unless the court directs otherwise, the judgment may be
/// signed if no specific objection is received from the adversary within
/// seven days of receipt of the prevailing party's judgment or order.
deadline proposed-judgment-objection-period: 7.days after ProposedJudgmentReceived() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 58.1(b)"

/// L.Civ.R. 72.1(c)(1)(A): a party appeals a magistrate judge's
/// determination of a non-dispositive matter within 14 days after being
/// served with the order; a timely motion for reargument under L.Civ.R.
/// 7.1(i) restarts the period from service of the order deciding it.
deadline magistrate-order-appeal-period: 14.days after MagistrateOrderServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 72.1(c)"

/// L.Civ.R. 72.1(c)(2): a party objects to a magistrate judge's proposed
/// findings, recommendations or report within 14 days after being served
/// with a copy.
deadline magistrate-report-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateReportServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 72.1(c)"

/// L.Civ.R. 73.1(d): the form consenting to trial before a magistrate judge
/// is filed not later than 21 days after the final pretrial conference.
deadline magistrate-consent-period: 21.days after FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 73.1(d)"

/// L.Civ.R. 201.1(h)(1): a demand for trial de novo is filed and served
/// within 30 days after the arbitration award is filed and served; the
/// period is 60 days in an action to which the United States or its
/// employee or agency is a party (below).
deadline trial-de-novo-demand-period: 30.days after ArbitrationAwardServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 201.1(h)"

/// L.Civ.R. 201.1(h)(1): in an action to which the United States or any of
/// its employees or agencies is a party, the demand for trial de novo is
/// filed and served within 60 days.
deadline united-states-trial-de-novo-demand-period: 60.days after ArbitrationAwardServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D.N.J. L. Civ. R. 201.1(h)"
